WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.708
BTRIM is excellent for boundary whitespace It
removes spaces from

00:00:05.734 --> 00:00:11.317
the start and end of a string But it does not
collapse repeated spaces

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:17.834
inside the value That distinction is important If

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:23.531
you need to normalize internal whitespace you need a
different function such as REGEXP_REPLACE with

00:00:23.557 --> 00:00:25.136
a repeated-whitespace pattern
